  "body": "Original: http://crbug.com/155566 from jeffbailey@google.com\r\n\r\nDo this program from an empty HTML file:\r\n\r\n```js\r\nvar div = document.createElement('div');\r\ndiv.textContent = 'foo';\r\ndiv.focus();\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe div correctly doesn't receive the focus, as the tabIndex hasn't been set.  However, the developer has no idea that this has happened, as focus doesn't return a value, nor does it display an error.\r\n\r\nMy ideal scenario would be to be able to receive an error programmatically so that I could tell in my code if this hasn't succeeded, but that might break a random site.  The more harmless second option is to display a warning on the console so that the developer can at least tell than an expected behaviour has not succeeded.",
